    "manas-2010:p1283:b001:l001": "This refers to the preceding attack and distress of Manas at1282:42; no new attack supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p1283:b001:l006": "Кыяматтык sworn friendship lasting to Judgment Day, the relationship in the rescue appeal.",
    "manas-2010:p1283:b001:l023": "Hair waist-cord and pierced intact part on24 are Kongurbay’s religious taunts; circumcision is implied without replacing the source euphemism with an invented ritual procedure.",
    "manas-2010:p1283:b001:l027": "Drawing the line retained literally as Kongurbay’s counterfactual claim before Great Beijing’s gate; exact ritual/action remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1283:b001:l036": "Captured hare is Kongurbay’s metaphor for Manas, not a new animal incident.",
    "manas-2010:p1284:b001:l015": "Digging my pit is the rebuke’s death/grave image, retained rather than an unprinted literal excavation.",
    "manas-2010:p1284:b001:l034": "Азоолок provisionally small in the comparison with the people attacked previously; exact lexical nuance remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1285:b001:l007": "The failed horse is the printed counterfactual condition; no negative removed to simplify the argument.",
    "manas-2010:p1286:b001:l016": "Akbaltay and Ulak Khan at19 retained as the printed patronymics; no harmonization to variant genealogies.",
    "manas-2010:p1286:b001:l031": "Saddle-shaped ridge is terrain. Aybanboz’s refusal to cross follows immediately.",
    "manas-2010:p1287:b001:l017": "Кара кашка тынар affectionate hawk comparison. Yudakhin lists the dark-marked subtype of тынар and figurative support/hope https://el-sozduk.kg/tynar-2/. No exact modern species identification asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1287:b001:l025": "Бейм uncertainty retained as I think, not converted into an unconditional curse.",
    "manas-2010:p1288:b001:l041": "Akkolpok is the named protective armor; gloss armor added to make the referent accessible, not a new item.",
    "manas-2010:p1288:b001:l042": "Akkelte is the named musket. The source’s spelling Аколпок/Аккелте remains unchanged in raw data.",
    "manas-2010:p1289:b001:l002": "Бүрүк uncircumcised, the source’s religious insult; not a botanical bud in this human epithet.",
    "manas-2010:p1289:b001:l009": "Twelvefold encirclement is the printed number, not a verified military formation.",
    "manas-2010:p1289:b001:l035": "Nest-mate retains the affectionate bond between Syrgak and Manas, without asserting literal shared parentage.",
    "manas-2010:p1290:b001:l002": "Parenthesized metanarrative verse retained and translated; not excluded as apparatus.",
    "manas-2010:p1290:b001:l003": "Visible жебеси point of the battle-axe retained; not silently replaced with a separate arrow.",
    "manas-2010:p1290:b001:l037": "Parenthetical praise on37–39 remains verse in source order.",
    "manas-2010:p1291:b001:l018": "Seventy wounds after seven days is the epic’s stated count, without physiological or chronological normalization.",
    "manas-2010:p1291:b001:l026": "Азил is documented as a variant of асил/асыл meaning root/origin/basis in Academy Манас эпосунун сөздүгү, 1995 (Abdyldaev, Akmataliev, Sadykov, Sarypbekov; ed. Musaev), АЗИЛ // АСИЛ // АСЫЛ entry, indexed primary PDF https://new.bizdin.kg/media/books/Словарь_эпоса_Манас.pdf. Applying root to faith is contextual and qualified; not silently emended to асыл or interpreted as ordinary joke. Indexed primary text consulted; direct PDF download returned404. Dictionary examples derive from Orozbakov, used lexically, not as Karalaev passage collation.",
    "manas-2010:p1292:b001:l015": "Whole-world scope remains on15; giants and their arrival remain on16. Cross-row sentence grammar does not transpose the source content.",
    "manas-2010:p1293:b001:l019": "Positive sparing his life retained beside the following lack of fear of death; no silent negative added.",
    "manas-2010:p1293:b001:l022": "Май кыл- stain/smear: exact Yudakhin entry quotes алтын тагын май кылып / атасы Азыз канды жай кылып and explains bloodstaining the golden throne while killing father Azizkhan https://el-sozduk.kg/май/. Not melting a throne.",
    "manas-2010:p1293:b001:l023": "Father’s killing on23–24 retained as explicitly stated here, despite divergent earlier narrative details; no claim to reconcile the epic variants.",
    "manas-2010:p1294:b001:l007": "Karazhoy’s shared study with Almambet retained; this does not independently identify a historical school.",
    "manas-2010:p1294:b001:l012": "Drawing a bow and firing shot are distinct source rows, both retained without forcing one weapon throughout.",
    "manas-2010:p1294:b001:l015": "Ninety wounds after nine days retained exactly; Chubak’s seventy/seven earlier is not substituted.",
    "manas-2010:p1295:b001:l008": "Турумтай merlin in the raptor/lark simile, distinct from the following ителги saker falcon.",
    "manas-2010:p1295:b001:l023": "Ten days’ journey is the stated distance, not an independently measured elapsed time.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l009": "Visible мурас inheritance retained, though goal would fit the battle context; not silently emended to мурат.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l020": "Бил elephant, Yudakhin/established lexicon, hence elephant-hide lance covering; no emendation to жыл.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l021": "Төкөр уста lame smith: exact Yudakhin төкө- entry translates төкөр уста төкөгөн as the lame smith forging the blank https://tamgasoft.kg/dict/index.php?lang=en&lfrom=kg&word=төкө-. Not deft or an unglossed title.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l026": "Festering injury is the fantasy weapon’s stated effect. The dragon venom and six immersions on27–28 are retained as narrative content.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l037": "Kökchebich is Syrgak’s named mount, not a young goat; тулпар rendered winged steed as epic praise, not a separate anatomical observation.",
    "manas-2010:p1296:b001:l040": "Outer and Innermost Beijing are the epic’s geographical distinctions; no modern boundary identification.",
    "manas-2010:p1297:b001:l007": "No holding back from combat and no alternative with Syrgak on8 remain separate rows; no extra negation inserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1297:b001:l029": "Visible reed lance retained despite its preceding formidable description and subsequent shattering.",
    "manas-2010:p1297:b001:l033": "Forty fragments retained as the stated count.",
    "manas-2010:p1297:b001:l041": "Ар кескен all-cutting blade corresponds to the recurrent nar-kesken form with initial-n loss documented in edition preface15; no extra weapon added.",
    "manas-2010:p1297:b001:l042": "The blade’s wielder is contextually Kongurbay, who severs Syrgak’s lance on1298:1–2; English retains the source’s unmarked subject shift.",
    "manas-2010:p1298:b001:l007": "Тамандашып provisionally feet braced in grappling; whether their feet press directly against each other is not asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1298:b001:l021": "Hair torn out and resulting baldness retained literally in the wrestling account.",
    "manas-2010:p1298:b001:l028": "Kongurbay’s prepared axe precedes the deceptive praise in the printed sequence; not moved after the later sleep.",
    "manas-2010:p1298:b001:l033": "Self-offering endearment repeated for lions and heroes at35; not independently described as an actual sacrifice.",
    "manas-2010:p1299:b001:l005": "Seven-day respite is Kongurbay’s proposal, repeated when Syrgak agrees at30; no elapsed week invented between those rows.",
    "manas-2010:p1299:b001:l013": "Shot-proof coat is Kongurbay’s promise within the epic, not a factual protective guarantee.",
    "manas-2010:p1299:b001:l025": "Own-hand bronze idol is the explicit religious claim in Kongurbay’s speech, retained without substituting a named deity.",
    "manas-2010:p1299:b001:l033": "Relaxing then briefly closing eyes then sleeping are all separately retained; not collapsed to an accidental blink.",
    "manas-2010:p1300:b001:l004": "Unmarked subject is contextually Kökchebich, named on5; horse made explicit to avoid attributing its evasive turn to the axe-striker.",
    "manas-2010:p1300:b001:l006": "Blow goes off target yet wounds the temple at14–15; this apparent tension is retained, not turned into complete escape from injury.",
    "manas-2010:p1300:b001:l020": "Даңкан clod thrown by hooves, exact edition glossary1836:b001:l031–033. Cauldron-sized clods are the source’s hyperbole.",
    "manas-2010:p1300:b001:l031": "Wild-sheep feet and copper forelegs are the horse’s praise images; not actual anatomical replacement.",
    "manas-2010:p1300:b001:l037": "Evil spirit seizing the wife retained as a simile for Kongurbay’s frenzy, not a separate reported incident.",
    "manas-2010:p1301:b001:l005": "Меке Mecca explicitly retained; not silently changed to Talas or a geographically plausible nearby destination.",
    "manas-2010:p1301:b001:l029": "Meadowsweet hollow and fescue valley at32 are Almambet’s affectionate comparisons for Syrgak.",
    "manas-2010:p1301:b001:l041": "Ribs torn apart expresses Almambet’s grief here; no added fresh combat injury.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l008": "Daughter-selling deceiver retains the curse; its target may be the treacherous world or Kongurbay, not automatically Syrgak.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l014": "Twenty years old retained as expressly stated; no correction to a reconstructed chronology.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l024": "Negative Beijing-land and Chinese-people comparisons retained with just to connect their rhetorical scope; exact compressed syntax remains qualified.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l027": "Visible белек gift retained in the fortified-place clause; no unprinted weapon or alternate place supplied. Precise figurative force remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l034": "Coming close to the three is retained here despite earlier apparent passage beyond them; no narrative reordering.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l037": "Күлүстөн affectionate garden/cherished-one image, Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/күлү/. Not an invented person named Külüstön.",
    "manas-2010:p1302:b001:l042": "Final cotton-belt/broad-boots formula continues into root1303; no invented conclusion to Syrgak’s speech."
  },
